`verilator_config
// DD105-B: what the waves leave out. pyuvm.mk passes this file to every build
// with TRACE=1 (the default). DD105-A's dd105_trace.vlt, without its UVM
// library line.
//
// The waves would otherwise include the package variable that says which
// planted bug is on (router_bug_pkg.bug_id, measured on the selftest's
// st_bug_pkg.bug_id), which gives a mystery bug away. So no package is
// traced; the design and the bound assertions are.
tracing_off -scope "*_pkg*"
// The router's faulty build reads +BUG in an initial block named bug_switch,
// whose local "id" holds the bug's number.
tracing_off -scope "*bug_switch*"
